occurrence is boxed as well: any intervening entry  x x  of  π \pi  with
 b < x < c b<x<c  would place both entries of its block inside the bounding rectangle
in  Δ ⁡ ( π ) \Delta(\pi) . 
 
 
 Conversely, let  a , b , c , d a,b,c,d  be a boxed  2143 2143  occurrence of  π \pi . It has the
unique boxed lift 
 

 
 
 2 ​ a , 2 ​ b , 2 ​ c − 1 , 2 ​ d − 1 . 2a,\quad 2b,\quad 2c-1,\quad 2d-1. 
 
 (25) 
 
 To see uniqueness, choosing  2 ​ a − 1 2a-1  would put its mate  2 ​ a 2a  immediately to the
right inside the rectangle; choosing  2 ​ b − 1 2b-1  would put  2 ​ b 2b  inside; choosing
 2 ​ c 2c  would put  2 ​ c − 1 2c-1  inside; and choosing  2 ​ d 2d  would put  2 ​ d − 1 2d-1  inside.
The choices in ( 25 ) avoid these obstructions. Their
unselected mates lie, respectively, to the left of the rectangle, below it,
above it, and to its right. Any other point inside the lifted rectangle would
belong to an intervening block  x x  with  b < x < c b<x<c , contradicting that the
original occurrence was boxed. Thus  φ \varphi  and this unique lift are
mutually inverse maps between the boxed  2143 2143  occurrences of  Δ ⁡ ( π ) \Delta(\pi) 
and those of  π \pi , proving ( 24 ).
∎ 
 
 
 
 Thus increasing doubling itself creates no additional boxed  2143 2143  occurrences.
It supplies a canonical alternating extension of length  2 ​ m 2m  whenever the
prescribed odd subsequence already avoids the pattern. This is not yet the
strict length- ( 2 ​ m − 1 ) (2m-1)  completion required by Conjecture  7.4 ; for a
general input, the remaining task is to arrange the even entries so as to
destroy the projected occurrences without creating new ones. 
 
 
 
